To catch a recruiter or hiring manager's eye, your portfolio landing page needs to present these audits as **high-value business solutions**, not just technical checklists. Accessibility hiring managers look for your ability to audit, prioritize, and systematically fix code.

Here is a clean, conversion-focused markdown layout for your portfolio landing page that presents your audits concisely.

---

**[Your Name] | Digital Accessibility (A11y) Engineer & Developer**

> **Specialist in WCAG 2.2 compliance, assistive technology testing (NVDA / VoiceOver), and semantic front-end remediation.**

---

**🛠️ Accessibility Audits & Remediation Case Studies**

**1. E-Commerce Checkout Flow: Critical Barrier Remediation**

- **Client / Site:** Retail Brand (Anonymised)
- **Scope:** 4-page checkout funnel with dynamic payment forms.
- **Initial State:** **34 automated violations**; checkout completely blocked for keyboard-only and screen reader users due to unlabelled custom inputs and broken focus management.
- **Key Remediation:**
  - Re-engineered custom select dropdowns into standard semantic forms with explicit `<label>` associations.
  - Injected accessible live regions (`aria-live="polite"`) to announce dynamic cart updates and inline validation errors instantly to **NVDA**.
- **The Result:** **Zero automated errors** remaining. Achieved **100% manual keyboard operability**, reducing cart abandonment risks for assistive tech users.

[View Full Audit Report (PDF)] • [View Code Before/After on GitHub]

---

**2. Corporate Web App: Mobile Navigation & Modal Overhaul**

- **Client / Site:** SaaS Platform Dashboard
- **Scope:** Main responsive navigation layout and dynamic data modals.
- **Initial State:** **High-severity keyboard trap** inside the mobile hamburger menu. Modals allowed keyboard focus to escape into the background page, confusing screen reader browse modes.
- **Key Remediation:**
  - Authored a robust JavaScript focus-trap script conforming to **WAI-ARIA APG patterns**, locking focus inside active mobile menus/modals and mapping the `Esc` key to exit cleanly.
  - Controlled dynamic states utilizing structural `aria-expanded` and `aria-hidden` attributes.
- **The Result:** Full compliance with **WCAG 2.2 SC 2.1.2 (No Trap)**. Smooth, logical linear navigation pathing for keyboard-only and power users.

